  "how_to_use": {
    "why": "Les patients à faible risque peuvent être de bons candidats pour le ténofovir, et les patients à haut risque doivent éviter le ténofovir lors de la détermination des traitements antirétroviraux appropriés.",
    "when": "- Patients chez lesquels un faible risque de survenue d'une CKD est attendu, afin de le confirmer\n- Patients chez lesquels un risque élevé de survenue d'une CKD est attendu, afin de s'assurer que des alternatives au ténofovir sont utilisées",
    "pearls": "- It is well-known that tenofovir is associated with a higher risk of developing chronic kidney disease (CKD).\n- This risk is substantially higher in patients with traditional CKD risk factors.\n- This risk calculator helps determine risk of developing CKD, and may help practitioners choose patients who would be good or poor candidates for tenofovir depending on their overall CKD risks.\n- This score was developed in a US VA patient population, and only males were included in this study.\n- This population was also overall “healthier” than the general VA population in other cardiovascular and renal disease states, with relatively low rates of hyperglycemia or hypertension."
  },
  "next_steps": {
    "advice": "",
    "critical_actions": "- Les patients ayant des scores faibles (0 point) peuvent être de bons candidats pour le ténofovir.\n- Les patients ayant des scores élevés (≥9 points) devraient éviter le ténofovir dans leur schéma thérapeutique, compte tenu de leur risque significativement plus élevé de développer une CKD dans les 5 ans.",
    "management": ""
  },
  "evidence": "",
  "more_info": "| Category | Score* | 5-year event rate (95% CI) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| TDF users | 0 | 1.4 (0.9, 2.2) |\n| 1 | 2.2 (1.4, 3.3) | |\n| 2 | 3.6 (2.9, 4.4) | |\n| 3 | 5.3 (4.4, 6.5) | |\n| 4 | 7.6 (6.6, 8.8) | |\n| 5 | 8.6 (7.4, 10.1) | |\n| 6 | 10.9 (9.4, 12.6) | |\n| 7 | 13.1 (11.1, 15.4) | |\n| 8 | 19.4 (16.3, 23.2) | |\n| ≥9 | 21.4 (18.1, 25.2) | |\n| TDF non-users | 0 | 0.5 (0.3, 0.9) |\n| 1 | 0.3 (0.1, 0.8) | |\n| 2 | 1.5 (1.2, 2.0) | |\n| 3 | 1.9 (1.4, 2.4) | |\n| 4 | 2.7 (2.2, 3.3) | |\n| 5 | 4.1 (3.4, 4.9) | |\n| 6 | 5.1 (4.3, 6.1) | |\n| 7 | 8.7 (7.4, 10.2) | |\n| 8 | 11.0 (9.2, 13.2) | |\n| ≥9 | 16.4 (14.1, 19.2) | |\n\n*Scores of 0 are considered low, while scores ≥9 are considered high.",
